From: SteamOS-Ubuntu <noreply@local>
Subject: [PATCH] wlroots: default case for newer libinput switch enums

LIBINPUT_SWITCH_KEYPAD_SLIDE is an enum value, not a #define, so
#if defined(...) never compiles the case and -Werror=switch still fails.
A default: label silences -Wswitch on Resolute and older libinput.

Apply from subprojects/wlroots with -p1 (against upstream 0.18).

--- a/backend/libinput/switch.c
+++ b/backend/libinput/switch.c
@@ -36,6 +36,10 @@
 	case LIBINPUT_SWITCH_TABLET_MODE:
 		wlr_event.switch_type = WLR_SWITCH_TYPE_TABLET_MODE;
 		break;
+	default:
+		/* KEYPAD_SLIDE (libinput 1.31+) and any future switch types. */
+		return;
 	}
 	switch (libinput_event_switch_get_switch_state(sevent)) {
 	case LIBINPUT_SWITCH_STATE_OFF:
